# Citation File Format — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# GitHub reads this to power the "Cite this repository" button.
# Maintainers: replace the author entry with the real author name(s) before
# release, and add a DOI under `identifiers` once a release is archived to Zenodo.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this book, please cite it as below."
title: "An AI-Driven Software Development System: A Theoretical Framework for the Modern Software Engineering Lifecycle"
abstract: >-
  A free, openly-licensed textbook on running a modern software development
  lifecycle when capable AI agents are first-class participants. Principles-first
  and vendor-neutral, it covers context engineering, token economics, governance,
  agent design, failure-first quality assurance, security, observability, and cost,
  with a running case study and a companion slide deck and test bank.
type: book
authors:
  - given-names: "Vivek"
    family-names: "Negi"
    # Add an ORCID if you have one (recommended for citation):
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-04-01"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/vivirony955/ai-driven-sdlc"
url: "https://vivirony955.github.io/ai-driven-sdlc/"
keywords:
  - software engineering
  - software development lifecycle
  - SDLC
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI agents
  - large language models
  - prompt engineering
  - AI governance
  - open educational resource
  - textbook
